@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
hide circle
hide empty members
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam componentBorderColor #40546A
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EAF2FC
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #E3F1D3
skinparam databaseBorderColor #40546A
skinparam ArrowColor #526579
skinparam ArrowFontSize 14
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 70
skinparam titleFontSize 24
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #F7F9FC
skinparam legendBorderColor #CBD5E1

title PolyNTU architecture\nFunctional modules

component "Participant browser\nReact-based frontend" as Browser
component "Market service\nquotes, trades, pricing,\nmarket lifecycle\n\nparallel unit: one HTTP request\neach request is its own task\non the multi-thread runtime" as Service
component "Settlement worker\nbracket scheduling, resolution,\nclaim settlement\n\nparallel unit: one market instance\nup to 8 settle at once, each in\nits own task; one market never\nsplits across tasks" as Worker
database "PostgreSQL\naccounts, markets, trades,\nevidence, ledger\n\nparallel unit: one connection\n32 pooled; row locks serialise\nwrites to the same market" as Db
component "External data sources\nconfigured resolvers and\nthe NTU bus feed" as Sources

Browser --> Service : trade, publish, resolve
Service --> Browser : live updates
Service --> Db : reads and writes
Worker --> Db : closes, resolves, settles
Worker --> Sources : fetches the outcome

legend bottom left
  One Rust process serves the browser and runs the settlement worker;
  both read and write the same database.
  The runtime has one worker thread per core and multiplexes tasks onto them.
  Requests split by request; settlement splits by market instance, never by
  account or claim, so one market's claims stay ordered under its row lock.
  Each open SSE stream is also its own task.
endlegend
@enduml
